NFS: Fix error handling for O_DIRECT write scheduling

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_10
commit-author Trond Myklebust <trond.myklebust@hammerspace.com>
commit 954998b60caa8f2a3bf3abe490de6f08d283687a
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_10/954998b6.failed

If we fail to schedule a request for transmission, there are 2
possibilities:
1) Either we hit a fatal error, and we just want to drop the remaining
   requests on the floor.
2) We were asked to try again, in which case we should allow the
   outstanding RPC calls to complete, so that we can recoalesce requests
   and try again.

Fixes: d600ad1f2bdb ("NFS41: pop some layoutget errors to application")
	Signed-off-by: Trond Myklebust <trond.myklebust@hammerspace.com>
	Signed-off-by: Anna Schumaker <Anna.Schumaker@Netapp.com>
(cherry picked from commit 954998b60caa8f2a3bf3abe490de6f08d283687a)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

